# Local development secrets for `next dev` / `wrangler dev` (via
# `initOpenNextCloudflareForDev`). Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored,
# never commit it) and fill in a real value.
#
# In production this is set with `wrangler secret put ANALYTICS_SALT` —
# never written into `wrangler.jsonc`.

# HMAC secret used to derive the daily-rotating, one-way `visitor_hash`
# stored against RSVPs/wishes/page views (see src/lib/crypto.ts). Any long
# random string works for local dev; a real deployment should use a
# cryptographically random value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
ANALYTICS_SALT=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# Bearer token required by `POST /api/cron/rollup` (see src/app/api/cron/rollup/route.ts
# and the README's "Analytics" section for how to schedule it). Any long
# random string works for local dev; a real deployment should use a
# cryptographically random value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CRON_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# Mailjet credentials for the RSVP/ucapan admin email notifications (see
# src/lib/mailjet.ts, src/lib/notify.ts, and the README's "Mailjet setup"
# section). Create an API key pair at https://app.mailjet.com/account/apikeys
# and validate a sender address/domain first — Mailjet rejects sends from an
# unvalidated `From:`. Left empty here on purpose: with these unset,
# notifications are a silent no-op (see notify.ts), which is the expected
# state for local dev and for a fresh clone that hasn't set them up yet.
MAILJET_API_KEY=
MAILJET_API_SECRET=

# Must be an email address/domain you've validated in Mailjet's dashboard.
MAILJET_SENDER_EMAIL=
MAILJET_SENDER_NAME=
